WEBVTT

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.339
♪

00:00:10.383 --> 00:00:16.302
[ snoring]

00:00:16.345 --> 00:00:18.304
[ gasping]:
Spiders!

00:00:18.347 --> 00:00:20.045
[ whimpering]

00:00:20.088 --> 00:00:22.177
Spiders... spiders.

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:23.309
They want me to tap dance.

00:00:23.352 --> 00:00:24.527
I don't want
to tap dance.

00:00:24.571 --> 00:00:26.094
You tell those spiders, Ron.

00:00:26.138 --> 00:00:28.140
Oh, yeah. T-Tell them.

00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:29.271
I'll tell them.

00:00:29.315 --> 00:00:31.143
I'll tell them tomorrow.

00:00:31.186 --> 00:00:32.448
[ snores]

00:00:32.492 --> 00:00:35.800
[ crunching]

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:47.855
♪

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:49.378
ROSMERTA:
Peter Pettigrew?

00:00:49.422 --> 00:00:50.815
McGONAGALL:
Little lump of a boy.

00:00:50.858 --> 00:00:52.512
Always trailing
after Sirius Black.

00:00:52.555 --> 00:00:53.687
FUDGE:
Black was vicious.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.341
He didn't kill Pettigrew.

00:00:55.384 --> 00:00:57.082
He destroyed him!

00:01:00.476 --> 00:01:02.217
[ snoring]

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:03.871
[ grunts]

00:01:03.915 --> 00:01:06.526
Put that light out.

00:01:06.569 --> 00:01:08.093
Sorry.

00:01:16.405 --> 00:01:21.454
♪

00:01:31.594 --> 00:01:35.033
♪

00:01:37.426 --> 00:01:39.472
[ panting]

00:01:42.431 --> 00:01:43.955
[ pattering]

00:01:43.998 --> 00:01:45.608
[ yelps]

00:01:47.262 --> 00:01:50.918
[ pattering away]

00:01:50.962 --> 00:01:52.137
Watch it there,
boy.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:53.965
We're trying
to sleep here.

00:01:54.008 --> 00:01:56.445
Yes, we are.

00:02:03.235 --> 00:02:04.889
Mischief managed.

00:02:04.932 --> 00:02:06.281
Nox.

00:02:07.456 --> 00:02:09.371
Potter.

00:02:09.415 --> 00:02:10.677
What are you doing

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.766
wandering the
corridors at night?

00:02:12.809 --> 00:02:14.507
I was sleepwalking.

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:15.725
How extraordinarily

00:02:15.769 --> 00:02:17.162
like your father
you are, Potter.

00:02:17.205 --> 00:02:19.947
He, too, was
exceedingly arrogant,

00:02:19.991 --> 00:02:22.602
strutting
about the castle.

00:02:22.645 --> 00:02:24.647
My dad didn't strut.

00:02:24.691 --> 00:02:26.214
And nor do I.

00:02:26.258 --> 00:02:27.999
Now, if you don't mind,

00:02:28.042 --> 00:02:31.959
I would appreciate it if
you could lower your wand.

00:02:33.613 --> 00:02:36.746
Turn out your pockets.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:41.186
Turn out
your pockets.

00:02:43.188 --> 00:02:44.319
What's this?

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:46.626
Spare bit of parchment.

00:02:46.669 --> 00:02:48.933
Really? Open it.

00:02:54.677 --> 00:02:58.420
Reveal
your secrets.

00:03:02.729 --> 00:03:04.687
Read it.

00:03:05.906 --> 00:03:10.476
"Messrs. Moony, Wormtail,
Padfoot and Prongs,

00:03:10.519 --> 00:03:16.482
offer their compliments
to Professor Snape and..."

00:03:16.525 --> 00:03:18.179
Go on.

00:03:18.223 --> 00:03:20.312
"...and request that he keep
his abnormally large nose

00:03:20.355 --> 00:03:22.967
out of other
people's business."

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.620
Why, you insolent, little...

00:03:24.664 --> 00:03:26.274
Professor.

00:03:27.449 --> 00:03:29.016
Well, well. Lupin.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:34.848
Out for a little walk in
the moonlight, are we?

00:03:34.891 --> 00:03:38.721
Harry... are
you all right?

00:03:38.765 --> 00:03:40.810
SNAPE:
That remains to be seen.

00:03:41.898 --> 00:03:43.204
I have just now confiscated

00:03:43.248 --> 00:03:46.164
a rather curious artifact
from Mr. Potter.

00:03:46.207 --> 00:03:47.556
Take a look, Lupin.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.602
Supposed to be your
area of expertise.

00:03:49.645 --> 00:03:52.692
Clearly, it's full
of dark magic.

00:03:52.735 --> 00:03:54.781
Oh, I seriously
doubt it, Severus.

00:03:54.824 --> 00:03:56.565
It looks to me as
though it's merely

00:03:56.609 --> 00:03:58.350
a parchment designed
to insult anyone

00:03:58.393 --> 00:03:59.394
who tries
to read it.

00:03:59.438 --> 00:04:01.440
I suspect it's
a Zonko product.

00:04:01.483 --> 00:04:04.443
Nevertheless,
I shall investigate

00:04:04.486 --> 00:04:06.358
any hidden qualities
it may possess.

00:04:06.401 --> 00:04:08.186
It is, after all,
as you say,

00:04:08.229 --> 00:04:09.665
my area
of expertise.

00:04:09.709 --> 00:04:12.016
Harry, would you
come with me, please?

00:04:12.059 --> 00:04:14.279
Professor,
good night.

00:04:19.023 --> 00:04:20.633
Are you deaf?

00:04:20.676 --> 00:04:23.114
Put that light out!

00:04:26.682 --> 00:04:28.206
Come in.

00:04:28.249 --> 00:04:32.079
Now, I haven't the faintest
idea, Harry,

00:04:32.123 --> 00:04:34.212
how this map came to be
in your possession,

00:04:34.255 --> 00:04:37.389
but quite frankly,
I am astounded

00:04:37.432 --> 00:04:39.869
that you didn't
hand it in.

00:04:39.913 --> 00:04:41.784
Did it never occur
to you that this,

00:04:41.828 --> 00:04:44.396
in the hands
of Sirius Black,

00:04:44.439 --> 00:04:46.398
is a map to you?

00:04:47.355 --> 00:04:48.313
No.

00:04:48.356 --> 00:04:49.705
No, sir.

00:04:51.751 --> 00:04:53.187
You know, your
father never set

00:04:53.231 --> 00:04:54.928
much store by
the rules, either,

00:04:54.971 --> 00:04:58.149
but he and your mother gave
their lives to save yours.

00:04:58.192 --> 00:05:00.673
And gambling
their sacrifice

00:05:00.716 --> 00:05:02.457
by wandering
around the castle,

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:04.764
unprotected with
a killer on the loose,

00:05:04.807 --> 00:05:08.550
seems to me a pretty
poor way to repay them!

00:05:08.594 --> 00:05:11.075
Now, I will not cover
up for you again, Harry.

00:05:11.118 --> 00:05:12.293
Do you hear me?

00:05:12.337 --> 00:05:13.512
Yes, sir.

00:05:13.555 --> 00:05:15.514
I want you to return
to your dormitory

00:05:15.557 --> 00:05:17.124
and stay there.

00:05:17.168 --> 00:05:19.648
And don't take
any detours.

00:05:19.692 --> 00:05:23.348
If you do... I shall know.

00:05:26.873 --> 00:05:29.093
Professor,
just so you know,

00:05:29.136 --> 00:05:31.051
I don't think
that map always works.

00:05:31.095 --> 00:05:34.402
Earlier on, it showed
someone in the castle.

00:05:34.446 --> 00:05:36.578
Someone I know
to be dead.

00:05:36.622 --> 00:05:39.625
Oh, really? And who
might that be?

00:05:39.668 --> 00:05:43.107
Peter Pettigrew.

00:05:44.891 --> 00:05:48.068
That's not possible.

00:05:48.112 --> 00:05:50.505
It's just what I saw.

00:05:52.812 --> 00:05:55.249
Good night, Professor.

00:05:56.946 --> 00:05:59.601
TRELAWNEY:
Broaden your minds.

00:05:59.645 --> 00:06:01.386
You must look beyond.

00:06:01.429 --> 00:06:03.736
The art of crystal gazing

00:06:03.779 --> 00:06:07.218
is in the clearing
of the inner eye.

00:06:07.261 --> 00:06:10.221
[ snoring]Only then can you see.

00:06:10.264 --> 00:06:11.526
Try again.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.920
Now, what
do we have here, hmm?

00:06:13.963 --> 00:06:17.532
Oh, do you mind me trying?

00:06:17.576 --> 00:06:20.231
Ah... ah.

00:06:20.274 --> 00:06:24.191
The Grim... possibly.

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:28.108
My dear, from
the first moment

00:06:28.152 --> 00:06:29.631
you stepped foot
in my class,

00:06:29.675 --> 00:06:32.243
I sensed that you
did not possess

00:06:32.286 --> 00:06:36.334
the proper spirit for the
noble art of Divination.

00:06:36.377 --> 00:06:37.813
No, you see, there?

00:06:37.857 --> 00:06:39.598
Ah, you may be
young in years,

00:06:39.641 --> 00:06:41.208
but the heart that beats
beneath your bosom

00:06:41.252 --> 00:06:42.862
is as shriveled
as an old maid's.

00:06:42.905 --> 00:06:45.691
Your soul, as dry as
the pages of the books

00:06:45.734 --> 00:06:49.216
to which you so desperately
cleave, mm-hmm.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:52.567
[ exhales]

